.TH RUN-FTPM-VIRT 1 "2026-11-17" "qemu-jetson" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
run-ftpm-virt \- boot the Jetson fTPM QEMU guest
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash scripts/run-ftpm-virt.sh
.RI [ mode ] " [options]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
Boots installed QEMU/firmware/Linux with the existing device identity, provisioning and disk.
Normal mode is the default and does not run tests or power off automatically.
Root has no default password. Root SSH and all SSH password authentication are disabled.
Use setup mode to create a regular user and register its public key locally.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B normal
Interactive Linux boot (default), no launcher time limit.
.TP
.B setup
Explicit initial-setup root console, not a root SSH login. No time limit.
Run adduser, add the user to sudo, and use qemu-register-ssh-key USER PUBLIC_KEY_FILE.
Power off when finished; do not expose setup consoles to untrusted users.
.TP
.B first, second, export, bound
Explicit automated test modes. First is only for a fresh test disk.
Tests default to FTPM_TIMEOUT or 300 seconds.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --setup
Select setup mode.
.TP
.BI --cpus " N"
1 to 8 CPUs, default 4. Requires firmware rebuilt for eight CPUs.
The launcher regenerates DTBs for the selected CPU count.
.TP
.B --ssh
Enable user-mode networking and forward 127.0.0.1:2222 to guest TCP port 22.
Normal/setup modes only. Requires guest openssh-server, a regular account and its authorized public key.
.TP
.BI --ssh-port " PORT"
Enable SSH forwarding on another localhost TCP port.
.TP
.BI --share " DIRECTORY"
Export one host directory using 9p with tag hostshare. Read-only by default.
Paths containing spaces are supported. Guest mounting is manual.
.TP
.B --share-rw
Allow writes to the exported directory. Requires --share and a guest --rw mount.
Host filesystem permissions still apply; mapped-xattr requires filesystem xattr support for writes.
.TP
.BI --timeout " SECONDS"
Override the mode time limit. Zero means unlimited.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Display usage.
.TP
.B --qemu-console
Multiplex monitor/serial on stdio; Ctrl-a c switches, Ctrl-a x exits immediately.
.TP
.BI --monitor-socket " PATH"
Create a monitor UNIX socket for a separate terminal. Exclusive with --qemu-console.
.TP
.B --gdb
Guest CPU remote debugger on localhost port 1234.
.TP
.BI --gdb-port " PORT"
Select another localhost GDB port.
.TP
.B --wait-gdb
Enable GDB and halt CPUs before firmware executes (-S).
.SH GUEST COMMANDS
.TP
.B sudo qemu-mount-host
Mount hostshare read-only at /mnt/host. No automatic mount or fstab entry is created.
.TP
.B sudo qemu-mount-host --rw /mnt/host
Mount writable, provided the host launcher used --share-rw.
.TP
.B sudo umount /mnt/host
Unmount the share.
.TP
.B sudo qemu-register-ssh-key USER /path/to/key.pub
Validate and append one public key for an existing regular non-root account.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bash scripts/run-ftpm-virt.sh
bash scripts/run-ftpm-virt.sh setup --ssh --share "$PWD/work/runtime-share"
bash scripts/run-ftpm-virt.sh --cpus 4 --ssh --ssh-port 2222
ssh -p 2222 cradsec@127.0.0.1
bash scripts/run-ftpm-virt.sh --cpus 2 --share /path/to/data --share-rw
.fi
.SH INSTALLATION
Fresh environment: follow docs/build-install.md, then initial user/key setup in docs/runtime-guide.md.
Existing environment: follow docs/upgrade-guide.md; preserve accounts, keys and TPM state.
Automated tests are documented separately in docs/test-guide.md.
.SH FILES
Installed boot artifacts: install/share/qemu-jetson/ftpm-virt/.
Mutable identity, provisioning and rootfs.ext4: work/ftpm-virt/.
Secure logs: work/ftpm-virt/secure-MODE-native.log (overwritten on the next same-mode boot).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
INSTALL_DIR overrides the install prefix. FTPM_SECURE_LOG overrides the secure log path.
FTPM_TIMEOUT affects test modes only unless --timeout is specified.
.SH EXIT STATUS
124 means a launcher timeout. Test success additionally requires the documented PASS markers.
Normal boot succeeds by reaching the intended guest service/login and shutting down normally.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR mount (8),
.BR passwd (1)
.PP
docs/build-install.md, docs/runtime-guide.md, docs/test-guide.md, docs/upgrade-guide.md
